# Cloud Network Lab — SSH client config
#
# Usage:  ssh -F <path-to-this-file> am-rtr01
#         ssh -F <path-to-this-file> rtr          (short alias)
#
# Names follow the convention in network-design.md: descriptive labels live on
# the VirtualBox VMs for humans, terse `am-<role><NN>` hostnames live on the
# machines for logs and DNS.
#
# Why this file exists: `ssh -o ProxyJump=host` does NOT reliably pass -i to
# the inner (jump) connection on Windows OpenSSH, so a one-liner ProxyJump
# fails with "Connection timed out during banner exchange" even when the jump
# host can reach the target perfectly. Declaring each host — including the
# bastion — gives the inner connection its own IdentityFile and fixes it.
#
# This is also just the correct way to run a bastion. The private key stays on
# the operator's workstation and is never copied to the jump host, which is the
# whole security argument for having a bastion in the first place.
#
# Cloud equivalent: the same pattern points at an EC2 bastion or is replaced
# entirely by AWS SSM Session Manager / Azure Bastion, which remove the need to
# expose port 22 at all. Phase 2 should compare the two.

# --- Router / NAT / DHCP / bastion — the only host reachable directly --------
Host am-rtr01 rtr lab-gw
    HostName            192.168.56.10
    User                erick
    IdentityFile        C:/Users/Erick/CloudLab/build/lab_key
    UserKnownHostsFile  C:/Users/Erick/CloudLab/build/known_hosts
    StrictHostKeyChecking accept-new
    IdentitiesOnly      yes

# --- Private-subnet hosts ----------------------------------------------------
# Unreachable from the workstation except through the bastion. That is the
# design, not an inconvenience.

Host am-app01 app lab-app
    HostName            10.0.2.20
    User                erick
    IdentityFile        C:/Users/Erick/CloudLab/build/lab_key
    UserKnownHostsFile  C:/Users/Erick/CloudLab/build/known_hosts
    StrictHostKeyChecking accept-new
    IdentitiesOnly      yes
    ProxyJump           am-rtr01

Host am-db01 db lab-db
    HostName            10.0.2.30
    User                erick
    IdentityFile        C:/Users/Erick/CloudLab/build/lab_key
    UserKnownHostsFile  C:/Users/Erick/CloudLab/build/known_hosts
    StrictHostKeyChecking accept-new
    IdentitiesOnly      yes
    ProxyJump           am-rtr01

# --- Domain controller — RDP, not SSH ---------------------------------------
# am-dc01 (10.0.2.40) has NO management NIC on purpose: a second adapter to the
# Windows host is exactly the private-to-management leak the security review
# flagged as F-02. Reach its desktop by tunnelling RDP through the bastion:
#
#   ssh -F scripts/ssh_config -L 13389:10.0.2.40:3389 am-rtr01
#   ...then point Remote Desktop at localhost:13389
#
# Cloud equivalent: SSM port forwarding or Azure Bastion. The convenient
# alternative -- a second NIC straight to the host -- quietly destroys the
# segmentation the whole lab exists to demonstrate.
